# Configuration for the Facebook Marketplace extractor.
# `just setup` generates .env for you; this file documents every option.
#
# The scraper needs an authenticated Facebook session. Two ways to provide it:

# --- Option A (recommended): reuse a logged-in Chrome profile ----------------
# Point at a user-data dir that contains a profile signed into facebook.com.
# The scraper launches Chrome with channel=chrome against this directory.
# On Linux/macOS the OS keychain decrypts the cookies, so the profile must be
# copied (not moved) from the same machine/user. `just setup` copies it to
# ~/.local/share/fme-chrome and writes these three lines for you.
#
#   FME_USER_DATA_DIR=/home/you/.local/share/fme-chrome
#   FME_BROWSER_CHANNEL=chrome
#   FME_PROFILE_DIRECTORY=Default

# --- Option B: email/password login ------------------------------------------
# Used only when FME_USER_DATA_DIR is empty. A captcha/security check must be
# solved manually in the browser window on every new session, so this is mostly
# a fallback for machines without a logged-in Chrome profile.
#
#   FME_USERNAME=you@example.com
#   FME_PASSWORD=super-secret
